    <h1 class="rv in" style="font-size:clamp(2.2rem,5vw,4rem);max-width:20ch">Can a Solo Traveller Book a Private Boat Trip in Madeira?</h1>
    <div class="artmeta rv in d1"><span>1 December 2026</span><span>5 min read</span><span>Funchal · Madeira</span></div>
  </div>
</header>

<section class="pad">
  <div class="wrap">
    <article class="article rv">
      <p class="lede">You can book the whole boat on your own, but know the cost first: Chifbay charges per boat, not per seat, so one guest pays the full 400 to 600 EUR. For many people travelling alone a shared trip makes more sense, and it is better to say so plainly.</p>

      <h2>Can one person book the whole boat?</h2><p>Yes. There is no minimum group size. You book the trip, the skipper meets you on the pontoon at Marina do Funchal, and the boat is yours: only you on board, on the same route and with the same inclusions as a group of five.</p><p>That means food and drinks on board, an Insta360 360 degree video of the trip, drone footage when the weather allows, photos taken with a real camera and, on the Day Trip, swimming and the paddle boards. Nothing is reduced because you are alone.</p><h2>What does it cost for one person?</h2><p>The same as for five, because Chifbay prices the boat, not the seats. The table shows each trip at its full price for one, and what the same price works out to per head if five people share it.</p><table><thead><tr><th>Trip</th><th>Length</th><th>Price for the boat, 1 guest</th><th>Same price split 5 ways</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Sunset Trip, turning at Cabo Girão</td><td>2h</td><td>400 EUR</td><td>80 EUR each</td></tr><tr><td>Sunset Trip, turning at Ribeira Brava</td><td>2h30</td><td>500 EUR</td><td>100 EUR each</td></tr><tr><td>Day Trip, 10:00 or 14:00</td><td>2h30</td><td>500 EUR</td><td>100 EUR each</td></tr><tr><td>Day Trip, to Ponta do Sol</td><td>3h</td><td>600 EUR</td><td>120 EUR each</td></tr></tbody></table><p>There is no single supplement and no discount for one person either. Whoever comes, up to five, the boat costs the same. For most solo budgets, that is a lot of money for two or three hours, and it is fair to weigh it honestly.</p><h2>When is it worth it on your own?</h2><p>When the private part is the reason you are going. A solo trip is not a cheap way to see the coast. It is a quiet, unhurried one, and a few situations make that worth paying for.</p><ul><li><strong>You want silence.</strong> No group chatter, no timetable set by thirty strangers. Just the engine, then the water at Fajã dos Padres when it stops.</li><li><strong>You are photographing the coast.</strong> Cabo Girão rises about 580 metres from the sea, and having the boat to yourself means nobody else is in your frame.</li><li><strong>You are marking something.</strong> A birthday alone, a big decision, the end of a long project. Some people want to spend that on the water, not at a bar.</li><li><strong>You want the footage.</strong> The 360 video, the drone shots and the camera photos are all of you, which is rare when you travel alone and nobody is there to take your picture.</li><li><strong>You swim at your own pace.</strong> On the Day Trip, the swim stops and paddle boards have only one user.</li></ul><p>If one of those is you, the <a href="/sunset-cruise">2 hour Sunset Trip</a> is the lowest price, at 400 EUR.</p><h2>What is it like to be the only guest?</h2><p>Calm, and as social as you want it to be. It is you and the skipper. Our skippers are local, so if you want to know which village is which, why the cliffs are terraced or what the fishing boats of Câmara de Lobos bring home, ask. If you would rather sit at the front with a glass and say nothing for an hour, that works too.</p><p>Travelling alone also means telling someone where you are. Send a friend or family member the trip time and the meeting point at Marina do Funchal before you go. You can also check the operator before booking: Chifbay is registered for maritime tourism as RNAAT n.º 305/2026.</p><h2>What are the cheaper alternatives?</h2><p>Shared trips sold per seat. Funchal has several, and for a solo traveller on a normal budget they are the sensible first choice.</p><ul><li><strong>Shared dolphin and whale trips.</strong> Catamarans and RIB boats run shared trips from Funchal. When we checked the big booking sites in November 2026, these were listed at roughly 35 to 55 EUR per adult for about 2h30 to 3h.</li><li><strong>The Santa Maria de Colombo.</strong> A replica of Columbus's ship that sails from Funchal, usually west along the coast towards Cabo Girão. It was listed at around 45 EUR per adult for 3 hours at the time of writing.</li><li><strong>Cabo Girão from above.</strong> The viewpoint and its glass skywalk are reached by road, if what you really want is the cliff and not the sea.</li></ul><p>Prices on booking sites change, so check the operator before you pay. Our comparison of a <a href="/posts/private-boat-charter-vs-shared-tour-madeira">private boat charter and a shared tour in Madeira</a> sets out what you gain and what you give up with each.</p><h2>Can you share the boat to split the cost?</h2><p>Yes, if you bring the people. Up to five guests can come, as one group, and the price stays the same, so every friend you add lowers your share. People you meet on a levada walk, in a hostel or on a food tour can make a good boat group, and a boat trip is an easy plan to share.</p><p>What we do not do is fill your boat with strangers. Only your group is on board, so one person books for everyone and you settle the split among yourselves. Free cancellation until 24 hours before the start gives a new group of friends some room to change its mind.</p><h2>Who should not book a private boat alone?</h2><p>Be honest about what you want from the day. Skip it if the price would hurt your trip budget, if you would rather meet people than have space, or if your main goal is to see dolphins. We never guarantee dolphins on our trips, and a dedicated dolphin and whale trip spends its time searching for them, while ours is built around the coast.</p><p>If you are still deciding, our piece on <a href="/posts/is-a-private-boat-trip-in-madeira-worth-it">whether a private boat trip in Madeira is worth it</a> walks through the same question for groups. Both of our trips are on the <a href="/experiences">experiences page</a>.</p><h2>Frequently asked questions</h2><h3>Is there a single supplement?</h3><p>No. The price is per boat, from 400 EUR for the 2 hour Sunset Trip, and it is the same for one guest or five.</p><h3>Can I join another group's private trip?</h3><p>No. Only one group is on board each trip. To share the cost, bring your own group of up to five.</p><h3>Which trip is cheapest for one person?</h3><p>The 2 hour Sunset Trip, turning at Cabo Girão, at 400 EUR for the whole boat. It has no swimming.</p><h3>Can I book a solo trip on GetYourGuide or Viator?</h3><p>Chifbay trips can be booked on chifbay.com and also on GetYourGuide, Viator and Click&amp;Boat.</p>

      <blockquote>Alone on the boat, the only voice below Cabo Girão is the sea.</blockquote>
    </article>
